estion/math-academy-id "q-87681" :question/problem "Solve the inequality $3-\\sqrt{x-1}<8.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we isolate the square root:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3-\\sqrt{x-1} & <8 \\\\ -\\sqrt{x-1} & <5 \\\\ \\sqrt{x-1} & >-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we had to flip the sign of the inequality since we divided by a negative number.\n\nHere, the square root is greater than a negative number $(-5),$ so any number we can substitute into the square root will satisfy the inequality. So, the solution is the domain of the square root.\n\nTo find the domain, we recall that the expression under the square root must be greater than or equal to $0:$\n\n$$\nx-1\\ge 0\\,⇒\\,x\\ge 1\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x\\ge 1.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-87681/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "24f2c5a5-dc56-5f78-8138-8f7b3a6280e2"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-87681"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-87682/selection/a2166b56ac9283a49c314c69ce026f1b812faf344000cc6010e9a213abf68628" :answer/id #uuid "6a0ea15f-f552-58c0-ac11-3db808bb4d05" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\le 1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-87682/selection/0edcb8165ab0c22fe54c451eb5dc608e5614ee48d575774cf2bb7897025b80e8" :answer/id #uuid "0f24499e-1383-57cf-8eae-e6fa2bb83692" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\ge -7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-87682/selection/14e4e7017f13777eef6e3281daf7a176fb620f472cfe8ae474e10eb34c3376ee" :answer/id #uuid "a1b98672-3647-5ead-b442-45ec7ffa1a5d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\le -3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-87682/selection/363ce6c464bca4061507ea80d1437a856d0c3af50026152be913a12886d76805" :answer/id #uuid "e57c30e1-b45f-5d0b-94da-cefe0c6162e9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\ge -3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-87682/selection/3cfc233d457edbec6b6deb35df070179afd90e6508c5585cd03e094cf600a715" :answer/id #uuid "b36b382f-8d51-53af-83b3-78bd61e8fead" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\ge 1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-87682/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "39ba0ef3-55c2-596e-9077-5c3996b511e7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-87682/selection/363ce6c464bca4061507ea80d1437a856d0c3af50026152be913a12886d76805" :answer-field/choices ["q-87682/selection/a2166b56ac9283a49c314c69ce026f1b812faf344000cc6010e9a213abf68628" "q-87682/selection/0edcb8165ab0c22fe54c451eb5dc608e5614ee48d575774cf2bb7897025b80e8" "q-87682/selection/14e4e7017f13777eef6e3281daf7a176fb620f472cfe8ae474e10eb34c3376ee" "q-87682/selection/363ce6c464bca4061507ea80d1437a856d0c3af50026152be913a12886d76805" "q-87682/selection/3cfc233d457edbec6b6deb35df070179afd90e6508c5585cd03e094cf600a715"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-87682" :question/id #uuid "6794d77b-d5bc-52f7-8666-e16b9e0bff8c" :question/math-academy-id "q-87682" :question/problem "Solve the inequality $4-3\\sqrt{x+3}\\le 10.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we isolate the square root:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4-3\\sqrt{x+3} & \\le 10 \\\\ -3\\sqrt{x+3} & \\le 6 \\\\ \\sqrt{x+3} & \\ge -2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we had to flip the sign of the inequality since we divided by a negative number.\n\nHere, the square root is greater than a negative number $(-2),$ so any number we can substitute into the square root will satisfy the inequality. So, the solution is the domain of the square root.\n\nTo find the domain, we recall that the expression under the square root must be greater than or equal to $0:$\n\n$$\nx+3\\ge 0\\,⇒\\,x\\ge -3\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x\\ge -3.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-87682/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "24f2c5a5-dc56-5f78-8138-8f7b3a6280e2"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-87682"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-115053/selection/a2166b56ac9283a49c314c69ce026f1b812faf344000cc6010e9a213abf68628" :answer/id #uuid "b0db2e2f-dd51-5285-bae9-7714789b537f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\le 1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115053/selection/8d8c6072938ecbfc07339cf484be979cce013a7675656b5ec57475808abcabbe" :answer/id #uuid "42a00f97-17d6-5781-b3c2-c517e6a2a502" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\ge -1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115053/selection/cf258055578efbcbb71802f9e8673ef3f675139bd1924918457d005805c2c913" :answer/id #uuid "d457b80a-0685-5505-9493-6872f3eabf07" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\le \\frac{9}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115053/selection/1c67eb2ef46586b192fb6f2404c9fcb638c457aea303fd3f00545632feeefccc" :answer/id #uuid "1a4b9d89-3ff5-54da-820b-eb021d5fe3e0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\le -4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115053/selection/bcba47e54b650a3c9e5d392521f7c50bf8afc71febba58027b0df3002859aeeb" :answer/id #uuid "05648092-eeca-52af-ad86-0c572122b53f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\ge \\frac{3}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115053/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "3d1bb207-997d-50fb-b711-479caefb0a09" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-115053/selection/cf258055578efbcbb71802f9e8673ef3f675139bd1924918457d005805c2c913" :answer-field/choices ["q-115053/selection/a2166b56ac9283a49c314c69ce026f1b812faf344000cc6010e9a213abf68628" "q-115053/selection/8d8c6072938ecbfc07339cf484be979cce013a7675656b5ec57475808abcabbe" "q-115053/selection/cf258055578efbcbb71802f9e8673ef3f675139bd1924918457d005805c2c913" "q-115053/selection/1c67eb2ef46586b192fb6f2404c9fcb638c457aea303fd3f00545632feeefccc" "q-115053/selection/bcba47e54b650a3c9e5d392521f7c50bf8afc71febba58027b0df3002859aeeb"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-115053" :question/id #uuid "db7eb34c-19dc-5bac-aefb-fd226ead4846" :question/math-academy-id "q-115053" :question/problem "Solve the inequality $\\sqrt{9-2x}-3>-4.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we isolate the square root:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{9-2x}-3 & >-4 \\\\ \\sqrt{9-2x} & >-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, the square root is greater than a negative number $(-1),$ so any number we can substitute into the square root will satisfy the inequality. So, the solution is the domain of the square root.\n\nTo find the domain, we recall that the expression under the square root must be greater than or equal to $0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9-2x & \\ge 0 \\\\ -2x & \\ge -9 \\\\ x & \\le \\frac{9}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x\\le \\frac{9}{2}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-115053/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "24f2c5a5-dc56-5f78-8138-8f7b3a6280e2"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-115053"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-115060/selection/ebe6f4d26afa362a416b64d63b5c4b51d9e2ae71005bcb2b10a9632f19911f50" :answer/id #uuid "3ba67780-950f-5ca0-b6fe-c6874b19b240" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\ge 2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115060/selection/1235061e5472926481ddeb36b23313e44d3189b3ae0ecc652c6bbec56a95bfe7" :answer/id #uuid "c8691714-11bf-5d6f-b408-dd725905dd83" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x>2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115060/selection/6f042c3786c43ccb1516863ae21b0e759ae7b9f7158fd9952ae9f3d0995af2d5" :answer/id #uuid "24e9e9cb-b2b4-563e-9932-cfa325a61465" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4\\le x<2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115060/selection/4fba1a1b5b5a88505fde9df3d3e0af291d4b393f60f86b1a594c882428959c7e" :answer/id #uuid "0bdc5ff1-eadc-511f-868d-7fbf1f58a122" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x<4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115060/selection/26cb08b47b4644c2aa447ee05782e7b4b3b16d3cfff096c0dec422a9a80eb3d4" :answer/id #uuid "b1e5f26a-8b86-5d1b-9905-5b8a2be8b11b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2<x\\le 4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115060/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "6c99caff-e9b9-51cb-9451-e28781324705" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-115060/selection/1235061e5472926481ddeb36b23313e44d3189b3ae0ecc652c6bbec56a95bfe7" :answer-field/choices ["q-115060/selection/ebe6f4d26afa362a416b64d63b5c4b51d9e2ae71005bcb2b10a9632f19911f50" "q-115060/selection/1235061e5472926481ddeb36b23313e44d3189b3ae0ecc652c6bbec56a95bfe7" "q-115060/selection/6f042c3786c43ccb1516863ae21b0e759ae7b9f7158fd9952ae9f3d0995af2d5" "q-115060/selection/4fba1a1b5b5a88505fde9df3d3e0af291d4b393f60f86b1a594c882428959c7e" "q-115060/selection/26cb08b47b4644c2aa447ee05782e7b4b3b16d3cfff096c0dec422a9a80eb3d4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-115060" :question/id #uuid "3e85dd46-e7c3-5897-aad1-f61ca46bc9a9" :question/math-academy-id "q-115060" :question/problem "Solve the inequality $\\sqrt{x+2}-4>-2.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we isolate the square root:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{x+2}-4 & >-2 \\\\ \\sqrt{x+2} & >2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this inequality, the square root is being compared to a non-negative number $(2).$ So, we can square both sides of the inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(\\sqrt{x+2})}^{2} & >{2}^{2} \\\\ x+2 & >4 \\\\ x & >2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we must only keep the solutions that are in the domain of the square root. To find the domain of the square root, we recall that the argument of the square root must be greater than or equal to zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+2 & \\ge 0 \\\\ x & \\ge -2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOur solution is $x>2,$ which can be expressed as $(2,\\infty ).$ The domain of the square root is $x\\ge -2,$ which can be expressed as $[-2,\\infty ).$ To find the solutions that are in the domain of the square root, we take the intersection:\n\n$$\n(2,\\infty )\\cap [-2,\\infty )=(2,\\infty )\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x\\in (2,\\infty ),$ which can also be written as $x>2.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-115060/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b9003081-7cf6-5a99-accf-6a69b65db47c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-115060"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-278283/field-1/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "3e544178-ab30-5a9a-ae0a-a927f900d259" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-278283/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "45b7203a-834c-5df9-b9e7-443f4f3330cc" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-278283/field-1/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer-field/choices ["q-278283/field-1/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-278283/field-2/f022eff7ecaa4435243255d76a2a932e99db9e71ca2b89b05fafca75800709a0" :answer/id #uuid "f56d7949-c7ac-5bc6-8fee-6b5d103a6a80" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\le" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-278283/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "ff6e0618-95f6-54cc-8fba-b44f8e952f66" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-278283/field-2/f022eff7ecaa4435243255d76a2a932e99db9e71ca2b89b05fafca75800709a0" :answer-field/choices ["q-278283/field-2/f022eff7ecaa4435243255d76a2a932e99db9e71ca2b89b05fafca75800709a0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-278283" :question/id #uuid "f2f0b8e2-445d-5900-a2e9-e7c3538ed57d" :question/math-academy-id "q-278283" :question/problem "Solve the inequality $\\sqrt{3x-6}-4\\ge -1.$\n\n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}\n$x$" :question/worked-solution "First, we isolate the square root:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3x-6}-4 & \\ge -1 \\\\ \\sqrt{3x-6} & \\ge 3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this inequality, the square root is being compared to a non-negative number $(3).$ So, we can square both sides of the inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(\\sqrt{3x-6})}^{2} & \\ge {3}^{2} \\\\ 3x-6 & \\ge 9 \\\\ 3x & \\ge 15 \\\\ x & \\ge 5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we must only keep the solutions that are in the domain of the square root. To find the domain of the square root, we recall that the argument of the square root must be greater than or equal to zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x-6 & \\ge 0 \\\\ 3x & \\ge 6 \\\\ x & \\ge 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOur solution is $x\\ge 5,$ which can be expressed as $[5,\\infty ).$ But the domain of the square root is $x\\ge 2,$ which can be expressed as $[2,\\infty ).$ To find the solutions that are in the domain of the square root, we take the intersection:\n\n$$\n[5,\\infty )\\cap [2,\\infty )=[5,\\infty )\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x\\in [5,\\infty ),$ which can also be written as $5\\le x.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-278283/field-1" "q-278283/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b9003081-7cf6-5a99-accf-6a69b65db47c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-278283"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
